00:00:03.429 --> 00:00:05.590 align:start position:0%
former malaysian prime minister najib  razak arrives in court for his appeal  hearing  last july he was found guilty of  illegally receiving about 10 million  dollars  from src international which was linked  to the state-owned investment fund 1mdb  the amount in this appeal is small  compared to the 1 billion  prosecutors say he's received from the  funds  najib who's been convicted on 7 charges  and still faces  35 more has denied all wrongdoings  i think his lawyers will argue that  number one he did not intend upon  those money coming in and number two if  they were coming in  uh then the the amounts of money would  be political contribution  last year najib said under oath just  before he was sentenced  he wasn't aware the money in his  accounts had come from src  international his lawyers argued during  the trial  he had been misled by a fugitive  financier low-tech joe  into believing the money was part of a  donation from the saudi royal family  the trial judge had dismissed the  defense argument describing it  as far-fetched the 1mdb financial  scandal  played a major role in bringing down  najib's party and its coalition  in a general election in 2018.  investigators say more than four and a  half billion dollars  were stolen from one mdb if he loses  this appeal najib still has a final  chance to challenge the conviction at  malaysia's top  court florence louis al jazeera kuala  lumpur
 

